# Response headers for the web client as a static site (Cloudflare Pages `_headers` format; Netlify
# reads the same format). An EXAMPLE, named so that no host picks it up by itself: copy it to
# client/dist/_headers after `npm run build:static` (DEPLOY.md, "Two services"), and replace every
# api.example.com below with your API's hostname. Nothing else needs to change.
#
# The Content-Security-Policy is the one the server sends when it serves the client itself
# (server/src/http.ts), with connect-src narrowed from any ws: or wss: to the API origin: the page
# may only talk to itself and to that one server, over https for the account API and wss for the
# socket. script-src stays 'self' with no 'unsafe-inline', which is what stands between an XSS bug
# and the refresh token in localStorage (client/src/lib/session.ts).
#
# script/e2e_split.mjs serves the split build with THESE headers, the API hostname swapped for the
# test server's, so a CSP that blocked the app would fail the end to end run.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; connect-src 'self' https://api.example.com wss://api.example.com; media-src 'self' blob:; img-src 'self' blob: data:; font-src 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'none'; object-src 'none'; form-action 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Permissions-Policy: microphone=(self), camera=(self), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()

/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
